//? Title: Counting Sort: Frequencies, End Cursors and Stable Identities
//? Subtitle: The original eight integers and named records, with actual native bucket and placement traces
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Counting sort uses a bounded integer key as an address. Frequencies determine
contiguous output blocks, cumulative counts supply their end cursors, and a
reverse scan places each input identity into its own slot. We retain the
original eight integers and eight named records, derive why this particular
placement is stable, and expose the actual native histogram, boundaries and
assignments. The record example sorts equal keys directly: arrival indices
travel as identities instead of being packed into larger, distinct keys.
Measured logical work separates the input length from the bucket range; checked
budgets expose the space cost before allocation. Narrow ranges near either
signed 64-bit endpoint work without overflowing signed subtraction.
)

\toc

> An eight-element problem with six addressable keys

Start with [2,5,3,0,2,3,0,3]. The inclusive range [0,5] contains six buckets,
although only four keys occur. Buckets for absent keys still take space and
prefix work. The sorted output should be [0,0,2,2,3,3,3,5].

Let L and U be the inclusive key bounds, k=U−L+1 and n the input length.
For bucket b=0,...,k−1 define its frequency, start and end:

\[
c_b=\#\{i:a_i=L+b\},\qquad
s_b=\sum_{r<b}c_r,\qquad e_b=s_b+c_b.
\]
\alttext(The frequency counts occurrences of a bucket's key. Its start is the sum of all earlier frequencies and its end is the start plus its own frequency.)

All copies of key L+b belong in the half-open interval [s_b,e_b). An empty
bucket has s_b=e_b. Here key 1 has interval [2,2), and key 2 begins at that same
position; there is no unused output slot between them.

The following complete program asks datamunge for the actual execution. Every
number in the native method diagram comes from that kernel's owned result.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/counting_sort_blocks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::counting_sort_trace({2,5,3,0,2,3,0,3},0,5);
  const auto& a=t.analysis;
  if(a.output!=std::vector<std::int64_t>{0,0,2,2,3,3,3,5} ||
     a.original_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{3,6,0,4,2,5,7,1}) return 1;
  std::print("| key | frequency | first output slot | initial end cursor |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=1.6;box.height=1.1;box.font_size=18;
  d.text({4.75,3.3},"Count keys, accumulate ends, then place backwards",23);
  for(std::size_t b=0;b<a.counts.size();++b) {
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",b,a.counts[b],a.starts[b],a.ends[b]);
    box.fill=a.counts[b]?dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254}:dm::graphics::RGB{243,244,246};
    d.node(std::format("count{}",b),{1.9*b,1.4},std::format("key {}\ncount {}",b,a.counts[b]),box);
    box.fill={254,243,199};
    d.node(std::format("end{}",b),{1.9*b,-.3},std::format("end {}",a.ends[b]),box);
    box.fill={220,252,231};
    d.node(std::format("block{}",b),{1.9*b,-2},std::format("[{}, {})",a.starts[b],a.ends[b]),box);
    d.edge(std::format("count{}",b),std::format("end{}",b));
    d.edge(std::format("end{}",b),std::format("block{}",b));
  }
  d.text({4.75,-3.5},"Half-open output intervals: absent keys have zero width",19)
   .save_svg("build/counting_sort_blocks.svg");
  std::print("\nSorted keys: {}. Original indices: {}.\n",a.output,a.original_indices);
}
```
