| output slot | name | unchanged sorting key | original index |
| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | Bob | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | Eve | 0 | 4 |
| 2 | Hal | 0 | 7 |
| 3 | Ann | 1 | 0 |
| 4 | Dan | 1 | 3 |
| 5 | Fay | 1 | 5 |
| 6 | Cy | 2 | 2 |
| 7 | Gil | 2 | 6 |

Unpacked equal-key identities match std::stable_sort: yes.
\image(figures/counting_sort_stability.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Colour identifies the actual unchanged sorting key. Each output group retains its original arrival order, as checked against an independent stable comparison sort.)
\alttext(Two rows show the eight named records before and after sorting. Green key-zero records Bob, Eve and Hal keep their order; blue key-one Ann, Dan and Fay do too; yellow Cy and Gil follow.)

A stable digit pass is useful in least-significant-digit radix sorting: after a
pass on a more significant digit, ties retain the order already established
by less significant digits. This report demonstrates the primitive, rather
than asserting that every radix implementation calls these particular overloads.

> Work is controlled by the whole range

Under the usual fixed-width integer RAM model, counting and placing cost n
iterations each, prefixing costs k, and zeroing the bucket arrays also costs
O(k). Bounds checks, optional automatic range discovery, owned result copies
and identity writes add O(n+k). Thus time and auxiliary storage are Θ(n+k)
for nonempty input; n=0 is a constant-time no-bucket case here. These counters
are logical work, not timings, total machine instructions or all memory writes.

Comparison sorting needs Ω(n log n) comparisons in the worst case over arbitrary
permutations of distinct keys. That lower bound does not say every input takes
that much work. Counting sort uses key values as addresses, so the comparison
model does not apply. Its range restriction is the price of that access.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/counting_sort_range_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> ranges,prefix,selected;
  std::print("| n | allocated buckets k | actual prefix steps | actual count + prefix + placement steps |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const std::size_t k:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024}) {
    std::vector<std::int64_t> input(128);
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<input.size();++i) input[i]=i%k;
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::counting_sort_analyze(input,0,static_cast<std::int64_t>(k-1),k);
    const auto operations=a.work.count_increments+a.work.prefix_steps+a.work.placements;
    if(operations!=256+k || a.work.range_items!=0) return 1;
    ranges.push_back(k);prefix.push_back(a.work.prefix_steps);selected.push_back(operations);
    std::print("| 128 | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,a.work.prefix_steps,operations);
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(ranges,selected,"count + prefix + place",{37,99,235},2)
      .line(ranges,prefix,"prefix only",{234,88,12},2)
      .legend({"count + prefix + place","prefix only"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Fixed n=128: unused buckets still cost prefix work")
      .x_label("explicit inclusive range width k").y_label("selected logical operations")
      .x_limits(0,1060).y_limits(0,1400).size(900,560)
      .save_svg("build/counting_sort_range_work.svg");
  const auto lo=std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min();
  const auto endpoint=dm::algorithms::counting_sort_analyze({lo+2,lo,lo+2});
  if(endpoint.original_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{1,0,2}) return 1;
  std::print("\nNarrow INT64_MIN range: k={}, permutation {}.\n",endpoint.counts.size(),endpoint.original_indices);
  bool buckets=false,events=false,invalid=false;
  try { (void)dm::algorithms::counting_sort_analyze({0,2},2); }
  catch(const std::length_error&) { buckets=true; }
  try { (void)dm::algorithms::counting_sort_trace({0,1,0},0,1,2,2); }
  catch(const std::length_error&) { events=true; }
  try { (void)dm::algorithms::counting_sort_trace({0,4},0,3,1,1); }
  catch(const std::invalid_argument&) { invalid=true; }
  if(!buckets || !events || !invalid) return 1;
  std::print("Complete bucket cap, complete event cap and full key validation: pass.\n");
}
```
